This repository is public so that people can read the work, evaluate the
engineering, and see how CLAWW is built. It is not open-source software.

1. What you may do
   - View and read the source code, documents and designs in this repository.
   - Clone or fork the repository, as GitHub's Terms of Service allow, to read
     it. A fork is for reading, not for running a product.
   - Review it to evaluate the authors' work (for example as part of hiring,
     collaboration, an academic or startup programme, or an investor review).

2. What you may not do without written permission
   - Use the code, database design, plan and meal logic, food and exercise
     data compilations, designs, text or images in any product or service,
     whether commercial or not.
   - Copy, modify, redistribute, sublicense, sell or host the code or any
     part of it.
   - Publish an app, website or service that is a copy of, or derived from,
     CLAWW.
   - Use the CLAWW name, logo, brand or domain.
   - Use the contents of this repository to train or fine-tune a machine
     learning model.

3. Third-party material
   Dependencies, fonts, data sets and tools used by CLAWW remain under their
